  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 315 AM EDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nWednesday night into Friday continues to look mainly dry with weak \nhigh pressure settling over the Ohio Valley. We will await the \narrival of a slow-moving shortwave trough riding over the western \nCONUS ridge. Highs in the mid and upper 80s will be common Thursday \nand Friday, with lows in the low to mid 60s. \n\nMedium range guidance is fairly consistent in bringing the upper \nlevel trough in from the northwest by Friday night. We then see an \namplification of the upper level flow, with the eastern CONUS trough \nclosing off and meandering nearby through the weekend. Look for \nincreasing chances for rain and thunderstorms over the weekend. \nIncreased cloud cover and precipitation should keep daytime highs \nsolidly below normal for the beginning of August.",
